I finally reached the top of the hill.
It was very quiet there.
I stood near the viewpoint.
The view in front was very beautiful.
I looked down at the deep valley.
Because of summer, there were dry and brown hills everywhere.
But that scenery was very grand.
A couple was standing next to me.
That man took some photos with his camera.
Then I took out my own camera from my bag.
I took many photos of that expansive valley.
A cool breeze was coming from the valley.
That breeze was touching my face.
I got completely absorbed in the nature there.
I lost track of time there.
I stayed there for almost two hours.
After that, the sun started to go down.
It was evening time.
I put my own camera back in the bag.
And I started the return journey.
